{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Confirmed RCA before repair: .github/mutation-shards.toml classified tests/**/conftest.py as global_support, and select_shards therefore selected all seven mutation shards for every nested conftest edit. Runtime tracing of every configured shard showed that pytest actually loads only six conftests in the selected tests ancestor chains; unrelated sibling fixture trees such as tests/external/live_jira_dc/conftest.py are never loaded. This rules out an omitted runtime fixture dependency and localizes the changeable defect to the recursive global-support entry. In 97 recent completed Verify runs, seven proven candidate over-triggers consumed 19,353 runner-seconds = 322.6 runner-minutes = 5.38 runner-hours. The intended behavior is dependency-accurate affected-test selection without coverage loss, supported by pytest upward-only conftest scope, Jest inverse dependency selection, and Nx explicit affected-input mapping. Repair evidence already completed: the final ancestry contract was RED against the original manifest (1 failed in 0.17s), GREEN after exact support mapping (1 passed in 0.56s), and two defect-seeded mutations both returned it to RED (missing interfaces ancestry and stale Jira DC support; 2/2 killed). The exact configured shard-test union remained 374 passed, 1 skipped. No dependency or test coverage was removed."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786750791922171001,"uuid":"1a191f13-ae06-417d-9a1c-f84c359c9e98"}